    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d750">

                <pb facs="1203" n="1107" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1107"/>

                <head>No. 747.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Robeson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 8,
                        1873</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Confidential.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose ten copies of
                    an arrangement made this day between me and the Spanish minister for the
                    surrender of the Virginius, and the survivors of those who were on board of her
                    when captured, and for the salute to the flag, should one be made, and ten
                    copies of the message of the President, with the protocol of the 29th November,
                    on the same subject. Referring to our conversation this afternoon, may I request
                    that the proper instructions may be given <pb facs="1204" n="1108"
                        xml:id="pg1108"/> without delay and in the manner indicated by you verbally,
                    or in such other way as may seem to you best, in order that the said arrangement
                    may be promptly carried out?</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S.—The copies referred to were delivered to Mr. Robeson personally this
                        p.m.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
